    "body": "### Problem\nWhen loading an existing wallet on a node where required blocks are not yet available on disk (for example, on a pruned node or during assumeutxo background sync before historical blocks are downloaded), `CWallet::AttachChain` previously registered `m_chain_notifications_handler` with the chain *before* validating block availability (`rescan_height != block_height`).\n\nWhen the availability check subsequently failed, `AttachChain` returned `false`, and `CWallet::LoadExisting` disconnected the notifications handler. Calling `DisconnectChainNotifications()` calls `chain().waitForNotifications()`, which drains pending validation interface callbacks. Any `BlockConnected` notifications queued on the scheduler or arriving from background synchronization during that window were delivered to the failing wallet instance. If a delivered block matched wallet transactions or fell on a periodic checkpoint, `CWallet::blockConnected` invoked `WriteBestBlock()`, persisting an updated `CBlockLocator` to disk despite the failed wallet load.\n\nAs a result, a wallet that failed to load was mutated on disk with an advanced locator. On the next load attempt after node sync completed, the wallet trusted this corrupted locator and skipped rescanning all preceding blocks, silently missing transactions and reporting incorrect balances (e.g. failing with `AssertionError: not(15.00000000 == 34)` in `wallet_assumeutxo.py`).\n\nFixes #36828.\n\n### Solution\nPerform the block-availability preflight check (verifying `chain.havePruned()` or `chain.hasAssumedValidChain()` against `haveBlockOnDisk`) before registering `m_chain_notifications_handler`. If required historical blocks are missing, `AttachChain` exits immediately with `return false` without ever registering validation callbacks. This ensures that no notifications are queued or delivered to the wallet, preventing any locator corruption or on-disk mutation during a failed load.\n\n### Testing\n- Built with CMake 4.3.0 and GCC 16.2.1.\n- Unit tests: Verified `test_bitcoin --run_test=wallet_tests,rescan_tests,walletload_tests` (32/32 test cases passed).\n- Functional tests: Verified `wallet_assumeutxo.py` passes cleanly (demonstrating that pre-sync failed load does not corrupt the post-sync balance).\n- Additional functional regressions: `wallet_basic.py`, `wallet_multiwallet.py`, `wallet_balance.py`, `wallet_backup.py`, `wallet_labels.py`, and `wallet_importdescriptors.py` all passed.\n",
