      "message": "wallet: check block availability before registering chain notifications in AttachChain\n\nWhen loading a wallet that requires blocks not currently available on disk (e.g., during assumeutxo background sync or on a pruned node), AttachChain previously registered m_chain_notifications_handler with the chain before checking whether required historical blocks were present.\n\nIf the availability check subsequently failed, AttachChain returned false, triggering DisconnectChainNotifications(). Disconnecting notifications drains pending validation interface callbacks, during which queued BlockConnected notifications could be delivered to the failing wallet instance. If a delivered block updated the wallet or matched a checkpoint height, CWallet::blockConnected persisted an updated best-block locator to disk via WriteBestBlock().\n\nConsequently, a failed wallet load could mutate the wallet on disk with an advanced locator. On the next load attempt after node sync completed, the wallet trusted this corrupted locator and skipped rescanning earlier blocks, silently missing transactions and resulting in incorrect balances (as observed in CI on wallet_assumeutxo.py).\n\nFix this by performing the block-availability preflight check before registering m_chain_notifications_handler. If required blocks are missing, AttachChain returns false without registering validation callbacks, preventing any notification delivery, locator corruption, or on-disk mutation.\n\nFixes #36828.",
